Antibiotic-Induced Acute Kidney Injury

1. Patient Details

Patient Initials / Identifier: B.T.

Age: 71 years

Gender: Female

Weight: 62 kg

2. Suspected Adverse Reaction

Description of Reaction: Unexplained oliguria (low urine output), rising serum creatinine (from 0.9 mg/dL to 3.4 mg/dL), and bilateral flank pain.

Date of Reaction Onset: Day 7 of antibiotic therapy.

Severity: Severe (Acute Kidney Injury Stage 2).

3. Suspected Medication(s)

Primary Suspect: Gentamicin 80 mg IV every 8 hours for complicated pyelonephritis.

Date Started: Day 1

Date Stopped: Day 8

Action Taken: Drug discontinued; switched to Ceftriaxone.

4. Concomitant Medications

Medication: Furosemide 20 mg daily (taken for heart failure; potential synergistic nephrotoxicity).

5. Outcome & Action Taken

Action Taken: Gentamicin stopped; aggressive IV hydration initiated.

De-challenge Outcome: Serum creatinine normalized to 1.1 mg/dL over the next 12 days.

Re-challenge: Not performed.

Patient Outcome: Recovered completely without lasting renal impairment.
